  "description": "VETO_THRESHOLD is configurable: with VETO_THRESHOLD = 2 a single veto does not disqualify, but it still flips the vetoer's standing vote to no",
  "spec_clause": "Phase 2 / Veto: 'Default VETO_THRESHOLD = 1; make it configurable, since one veto is right for five friends and too strict for twenty.' + 'Vetoing sets the voter's standing vote on that movie to no'",
  "rationale": "Identical Phase 1 setup to V019 (m1 yes 4 / approval 1.00, m2 yes 3 / 0.75, m3 yes 2 / 0.50, all eligible and promoted), but VETO_THRESHOLD = 2. u4 vetoes m1: vetoes(m1) = 1 < 2 -> NOT disqualified. All three finalists survive, so the full round robin is 3 pairs: m1 beats m2 4-0, m1 beats m3 4-0, m2 beats m3 3-1. Copeland m1 = 2, m2 = 1, m3 = 0; m1 beats every other finalist -> Condorcet winner m1, i.e. the movie u4 vetoed still wins because the group is configured to need two vetoes. The standing-vote side effect still applies: u4's yes on m1 becomes no.",
